{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And now my soul pours out upon me</b> — the near meaning [is]: for the opposite is upon all terrors, and all terrors pursue my noble spirit — and it is my soul, as in: 'and a noble spirit sustains me' (Psalm 51:14)." "<b>Like a cloud that passed</b> — thus my salvation passed, and now therefore my soul pours out upon me, for the days of my affliction seize me."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:02.332272194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}